// Quick-Edit mode workflow. id = "quick-edit".
//
// Toggle it with the auto-registered Main-section action:
//   FTS_INPUT_WORKFLOW_QUICK_EDIT  ("Workflow: Quick-Edit")
//
// On  → lower-half item drag becomes slip edit (move item contents), and
//       snapping is turned off so the slip ignores snap.
// Off → the mouse modifier and the snap setting are restored.
//
// REAPER's lower-half context has no dedicated "slip ignoring snap" behavior,
// so "ignoring snap" is achieved by disabling global snapping while active.

name        "Quick-Edit"
description "Fast item editing: lower-half drag slips item contents, snapping off."

mouse_overlays (quick-edit)

settings (
    {command 1157, enabled false, desc "Disable snapping (so slip ignores snap)"}
)

// Arm "Split item under mouse cursor (select right)" while quick-edit is on
// (disarmed on toggle-off). One click-drag = split + slip the right piece:
//   intercept_clicks → FTS catches the item mouse-down and runs the split.
//   slip_drag        → FTS then drives the slip itself, dragging the right
//                      piece's take contents as the mouse moves, until release.
// We drive the slip rather than passing the click through to REAPER's native
// slip because the fresh split boundary lands under the cursor — REAPER would
// read that as an item-EDGE drag (trim), and no mouse-modifier maps an edge to
// slip. Driving it ourselves sidesteps edge-detection entirely.
armed_action {command 42577, name "Split item under mouse (select right)", intercept_clicks true, slip_drag true}
